    "body": "Follow-up to #2. Its successful public CI run39675017845 (5 structured-data and166 full-suite checks) recorded PNPM storage at `/home/runner/.local/share/pnpm/store/v11`. This violates the owning-section data rule.\n\nThe same original workflow now receives canonical owned data paths before effects and binds Corepack, npm/PNPM, all four XDG selectors and temporary files below `data/logs/publisher-entity-ci-logs/`. Installation uses an explicit PNPM store and receives its actual canonical location. Authored HOME stays inherited. Original action pins, permissions, test commands, frozen dependency selection and12minute bound remain unchanged. All other source is cryptographically preserved by the original Git immediate-tree proof.\n\nIndependent exact-source review received ff19177a; existing YAML and shell syntax checks passed. The original public standard-runner job must now receive installation, the actual owned store and the full unchanged tests in this corrected context. No private CI, manual rerun, release or deployment is claimed.\n\n<!-- 561-github-review-call:50352317c10076d5f924181a64d2d9f904b012b9f8c14fb7b876d776435d553a -->",
